History note (license change at v0.20.7+):

Versions of One Link prior to commit `87d1b98` (released as
v0.20.7+ in 2026-05) were distributed under the MIT License.
Those releases remain under MIT, in perpetuity, by the original
copyright holder — anyone in possession of an MIT-licensed
release retains every right MIT granted them.

Starting with the AGPLv3 license commit, all NEW contributions
and NEW derivative works are governed by AGPLv3.  The change is
deliberate and described in NOTICE: One Link is for the people,
and AGPLv3 is the license that ensures forks built on top of
One Link's privacy work can't be quietly enclosed inside a
corporate product without sharing those modifications back to
the people who use them.

If you forked or built on the MIT version: nothing about your
fork changes; you may continue under MIT until you choose to
sync with a post-AGPLv3 commit (at which point AGPLv3 covers
your sync).
